Gas-n-Go is a chain of auto body shops in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]]. Its shop at 412 Anchor Boulevard in [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/index|Widdershins]] is a small one-story building on a busy street of through traffic: gas pumps under an awning out front, a garage of three bays to one side, a counter and a store level inside, and alleys with dumpsters and a service door down the left side. The shop is closed now, its shutters down, and inquisitors of the [[Org/Iridescent Church/Convox/Inquisition/index|Inquisition]] in purple armor hold the store level and the fane beneath it.

Under the shop, past a back door on the store level, is a [[Hearts|Heart]]'s fane, and none of it matches the shop above. A spiral stair turns counterclockwise between stained glass showing one continuous fire, the air is warm, and the floor and inner wall are dull steel plating with pneumatics moving beneath them, like the building breathing. The stair is narrow enough for one person at a time. At its foot, a steel-and-glass hall leads to a glass bridge over a gap, with a throne on a raised altar at the far end.

The fane was the hideout of the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] and of [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]], who is dead.

Below the throne room the fane continues into a seven-sided antechamber, a door set in each of its six outer walls. In the center, a foot off the ground, a five-foot chunk of obsidian turns slowly clockwise, threaded with veins of stained glass that widen as you watch. The voice of the fane's [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/An Iron Gauntlet in a Glass Glove|Heart]] comes out of the rock.

Each door is a wrought-iron arch nine feet tall, fronted with stained glass. Behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]]'s door is Tywelwyn's bedroom, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]]'s the armory, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]]'s the radar dish plant and the room where he prepared for the pilgrimage, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]]'s his office, behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]]'s a haberdasher, and behind [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]]'s an orrery.

The bedroom holds a wide four-post bed with mirrors above it and a wardrobe of eight identical capes, alongside a black robe three sizes too large for Tywelwyn. The armory keeps firearms in lockers and shelves. The office is cramped and plain next to the rest of the fane: a typewriter, tables of papers, and wheeled chalkboards drawn with a map of [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/index|Hallia]] and with musical notation. Many of its papers and ledgers are gone, carried off by the Party.
